  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 131 PM MDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nSeeing showers and isolated thunderstorms again in the southern\nmountains this afternoon and evening. May see a few elsewhere\nbut mainly not expected to reach the ground in lower elevations.\nExpect a return of isolated showers and thunderstorms once again\nWednesday afternoon and evening again southern mountains as well\nas central mountains so areas beginning to increase. Will start\nto see some cooling Wednesday with highs mainly in the 80s to\nlower 90s low elevations and 70s and 80s mountains. The\nmonsoonal moisture is really expected to push into all of\nsoutheast Idaho Thursday on strong southwest flow aloft with\nhigh precipitation chances both Thursday and Friday. Likely\nprecipiation amounts of 0.10 to 0.50 in the eastern Magic Valley\nand Snake River Plain and 0.25 to 0.80 inches in high elevations\nthe most likely amounts. There are of course very low percent\nchances of more at some high elevation locations on both days.\nWill be much cooler Thursday and Friday with low elevation highs\nin the 70s and mountains mainly in the 60s. Precipitation will\ndiminish Saturday but still widespread in the eastern \nmountains, with only isolated coverage Sunday through next \nTuesday. Will start to warm to near normal temperatures by early\nnext week with mainly 70s mountains and 80s valleys.",
